<title>SINGAPORE: Van Der horst full year net up 7.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Van Der horst full year net up 7.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     52.6    vs     48.96</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	    48.9    vs     47.9</p>
<p>    Turnover			130.39   vs    220.97</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)	    3.5    vs	3.0</p>
<p>    Investment Income	     0.14   vs	0.46</p>
<p>    Other Income		    6.75   vs     10.48</p>
<p>    Interest Expense		3.31   vs	2.41</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation   3.89   vs	4.73</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		 54.67   vs     51.15</p>
<p>    Profit from associates	0.84   vs	0.59 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				 2.89   vs	1.72</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries  (loss)     0.72   vs	nil</p>
<p>Note - Van der Horst Ltd is an infrastructure engineering company with substantial business interests in Indonesia.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
